================================================================================
SWRL -> SHACL regression test coverage
================================================================================

Context:
Following the removal of the legacy SWRL engine (SHACL-AF now executes the
IF/THEN business-rules UI), we hardened the test suite with a dedicated
regression suite that pins the SWRL -> SHACL-AF behavioural contract so any
future drift away from the legacy semantics is caught. The suite complements
test_shacl_rule_engine.py (which asserts *that* SQL is emitted) by nailing
down *what* that SQL means and *what* the engine returns, across the full
capability battery (unary/binary atoms, property chains, comparison + string
built-ins, closed-world negation).

Changes:
1. tests/units/reasoning/test_swrl_to_shacl_regression.py (new, 22 tests) —
   - TestEngineContractParity: end-to-end via a canned triple store —
     `stats["phase"] == "swrl"` / `engine == "shacl-af"`, `swrl:<rule>`
     provenance, enabled-only rules_count vs rules_total, disabled rules emit
     no SQL, whole-battery error-free run, materialisation INSERT +
     `swrl:materialized` marker, focus restricts to the entity URI, and
     inference_limit is applied.
   - TestInferenceSqlSemantics: the SQL each capability compiles to —
     property-chain derives the relationship head with closed-world NOT EXISTS
     de-dup; comparison built-in classifies via rdf:type HighValue with an
     ANSI-safe TRY_CAST filter; string built-in translates `contains` to
     LIKE CONCAT without leaking the built-in predicate; class-only rule is a
     classification no-op (no inference SELECT); negation has no positive
     inference SELECT and renders its closed-world body as nested NOT EXISTS
     in the violation query.
   - TestDialectParity: across the whole battery, Postgres SQL leaks no
     Spark-only syntax (TRY_CAST / RLIKE / CURRENT_TIMESTAMP()) and Spark SQL
     leaks no Postgres-only syntax (::float8 / ::double precision).
   - TestTranspilerClassificationParity: stable sh:TripleRule vs sh:SPARQLRule
     mapping per capability, antecedent-class targeting, CONSTRUCT bodies on
     SPARQL rules, and FILTER NOT EXISTS for negation.
   - TestShaclViewParity: the new read-only SHACL view (serialize) and the
     editor preview render every capability (one sh:NodeShape per rule under a
     single shared header; preview returns well-formed turtle + rule_type).

Modified files:
- tests/units/reasoning/test_swrl_to_shacl_regression.py (new)

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m 'not scenario' -> 10184 passed, 325
skipped (the new suite adds 22). Focused business-rules run
(tests/units/reasoning + tests/units/ontology + test_routes.py +
test_swrl_text_pane.py) -> 1248 passed. The only full-suite failure is
test_size_budget.py (agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py::run_agent 198->200),
verified pre-existing and unrelated to this change.
